  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing due to data volume full \u2014 not app, permission or db.\n\n**Root cause: filesystem holding uploads is full**\n\n* `POST /upload` returns `500 Internal Server Error` with `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device` in `out.write(chunk)` at `/app/main.py line 59` (E3). Earlier `POST /upload 200 OK` in same log shows this is new failure (E3).\n* `/srv/lab-data` \u2014 `use_percent 99.9`, `available_mb 0.4` of `size_mb 487.2` (E4). Inodes fine at `0.3%` (E4) \u2014 block-space exhaustion.\n* Root filesystem separate and healthy: `use_percent 6.8`, `available_mb 91424.0` on `/` (E6), `mountpoint /srv/lab-data` distinct from `/` (E4). Rules out host root-full.\n\n**Symptom vs cause:**\n500 on upload is symptom (E3). Cause is storage, not app code \u2014 `/health` still `200 {\"status\":\"ok\"}` (E2).\n\n**Ruled out:**\n\n* Permissions: `/srv/lab-data/uploads is_dir true`, `owner 1000:1000`, `mode 0755`, `app_uid 1000`, `app_user_can_write true` (E5). Parent `/srv/lab-data` same `can_write true` (E11). App runs as `1000:1000` (E7) \u2014 matches.\n* Mount: `incidentlab-app-1 running true`, `bind source /srv/lab-data destination /data rw true` (E7), `restart_count 0`, `oom_killed false`, `exit_code 0` (E7).\n* DB dependency: `incidentlab-db-1 running Up healthy` (E1), `inspect health healthy running true restart_count 0 oom_killed false` (E10), `LOG: database system is ready to accept connections` (E9), same `incidentlab_default` network as app (E7, E10). No DB error in app traceback (E3).\n* Crash-loop: `recent_events` shows only clean `kill/stop/die exit 0/destroy/rename/start` recreates and `health_status: healthy` (E8), not error restarts.\n\nBoth containers `running` (E1).\n\nRepair needs free/clean space on `/srv/lab-data` \u2014 no repair done.\n",
